"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The project has received a $2M budget approval and is expanding its team with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, joining in an onboarding session on September 10th. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase using AI algorithms, to be discussed on August 5th. The project has successfully completed its design and testing phases, with a prototype for secure file sharing tested ahead of schedule. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. The team is now moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, with UI enhancements planned for October. A milestone celebration is scheduled for October 10th."
